## Review fixes (semantic_reviewer, /projects/sandbox/reviews/pr1477.md)
$ npx vitest run src/hooks/useJumpToMessage.test.ts src/components/messages/ConversationView.reply-jump.vtid-05318.test.tsx src/pages/messages/GroupChat.reply.vtid-05318.test.tsx   # 8 + 5 + 6 passed; the 4 new group tests fail on the pre-fix GroupChat
$ npx vitest run src/components/messages src/pages/messages src/hooks src/lib/messaging   # all green
Fixed: only jump rows OLDER than the loaded rows are shown (withJumpRows) — a delete/edit/realtime update of loaded rows always wins, a deleted message never comes back; group edits/deletes also apply to jump rows; the jump releases the bottom-follow (DM isUserNearBottomRef, group pin) so growing content can't pull it back; a late group window is dropped after a group switch; the reply preview resets on group switch; group voice/attachment sends answer the open preview; swipe-to-reply in groups (phone); abandoned quote fetches are retried on the next visit (no stuck "loading"); paging back from a DM jump window uses the window's oldest row (?before=); legacy group threads in the DM view jump quietly to rendered rows only; a repeat tap restarts the highlight; DM reply send carries the parent id (test).
Deviation for Gate 2: plan I8 says "replace the window"; the lane keeps the latest page and bridges forward (?after=, now up to 10 pages = 1000 rows). Beyond that a gap can remain between the window and the latest page (rare: > 1000 messages between).

## Follow-up review fixes (/projects/sandbox/reviews/pr1484.md)
$ npx vitest run src/hooks/useJumpToMessage.test.ts src/components/messages/ConversationView.reply-jump.vtid-05318.test.tsx src/pages/messages/GroupChat.reply.vtid-05318.test.tsx   # 8 + 6 + 6 passed
Fixed: DM edit/delete also update rows shown only from a jump window (test; fails without the fix); the bridge now reaches the NEWEST loaded row, so when the latest page moves on no hole opens (copies stay hidden until then — test); a network/server error leaves a quote unresolved (retried) instead of "not available"; DM quotes beyond the first 10 are fetched in further batches; paging back from a DM jump window stops at the start of the conversation; a jump abandoned by switching conversation shows no toast and writes nothing (DM and group).
Remaining (low, accepted): other members' edits/deletes of rows shown only from a jump window appear after reopening the conversation.
